      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. I'll improve understandability by:\n1. Removing all unused imports and class-level constants\n2. Renaming the opaque local variable `test` → `original`\n3. Extracting the deserialized result to a named variable for clarity\n4. Adding a focused comment explaining *why* `assertSame` is used (the `readResolve` singleton cache)The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removing all unused imports and class-level constants, renaming the local variable `test` to `original` for clarity, extracting the deserialized result into a named `deserialized` variable, and adding a comment above the test explaining why `assertSame` is expected to hold (due to `DayOfYear`'s `readResolve()` returning the cached singleton)."
